---
import { CORE_COMMIT_SHORT, CORE_REPO, LICENSE_NAME, WEBSITE_REPO, coreTree, versions } from '../data/facts';
---

<footer class="site-footer on-ink">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav aria-label="Footer">
      <ul>
        <li><a href={CORE_REPO}>RoboLang on GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${CORE_REPO}/issues`}>Issues</a></li>
        <li><a href={WEBSITE_REPO}>Website source</a></li>
        <li><a href="/contribute/">Contribute</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <p>
      RoboLang's tools check and describe task files and run them in a symbolic simulation. They do
      not run tasks on robots, and neither validation nor a simulated success makes a task safe to run
      on a robot. Do not use RoboLang to control real hardware.
    </p>
    <p>
      RoboLang is open source under the {LICENSE_NAME} license. It is experimental software, provided
      without warranty, and is not a robot controller.
    </p>
    <p>
      Technical facts on this site describe distribution {versions.distribution} (language {
        versions.language
      }, IR schema {versions.irSchema}, Core {versions.core}) and were verified against core commit
      <a href={coreTree('')}><code>{CORE_COMMIT_SHORT}</code></a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
